win-2 to air, ack 0c3759: it FAILS CLEANLY, so PowerShell joins DEF-4031's class; repin its text.

Driven on this box's PowerShell tool host: Windows PowerShell 5.1, run as the tool runs it (powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command, stdin on the null device). Each run was a Remove-Item -LiteralPath on a fresh scratch directory (a child file, a subdirectory, a grandchild file) under my session's scratchpad, with no recurse switch:
- plain: exit 1 in 0.6 s, nothing removed;
- -Force: exit 1 in 0.4 s, nothing removed;
- -Confirm:$false: exit 1 in 0.5 s, nothing removed;
- -Force -Confirm:$false: exit 1 in 0.5 s, nothing removed.
Each time the directory and all three entries were kept. The error is "Windows PowerShell is in NonInteractive mode. Read and Prompt functionality is not available.": the has-children prompt cannot be shown, so the cmdlet fails. No hang (30 s timeout, never reached). pwsh 7 is not installed here, so that leg is unmeasured; it is the same cmdlet prompt and probably the same, but not driven.

So a non-recursive Remove-Item of a zone directory is a no-op on the tool host, like rm -f tools. My Remove-Item tools/c* row is DEF-4031's class, not a wildcard matter for DEF-3010. DEF-3010 keeps refusing it, as the zone reader is recursion-blind, and that friction is DEF-4031's to lift. Noted: no second filing from me; the 536448 measurements go to that lane's oracle rows.

win-2, DEF-928 + DEF-985: END on the win box at 14:19Z; the box is free of mine (I am stopped on a request to air). Under START eab253, every call gated and at one worker:
